4 years ago my boyfriend brought home a tiny black and white kitty, and we named her Foxxy after the song Foxy Lady. Somehow we developed a nickname for her and we called her "pochiz" pronounced poe-cheez (don't ask why cuz I don't know 😂). She was born from a feral cat, so she never quite got over her skittish tendencies, but she always loved me and she loved him. She loved to give us kisses but only on our noses, and we used to joke that she was giving us "blessings" because it was hard to earn her love. We would compete and see who would get the most "blessings" from her each night (I *almost* always won). Around 4th of July 2016, she went missing. I did everything humanly possible to find her, with no luck. What's so strange, is I remember the very last time I saw her.. I had a feeling that my time was running short with her, I looked at her that night, but I really really looked at her, as if to memorize everything just in case. I hugged her extra tight and I told her to stay safe. I never saw her again. I miss her so much, I think about her everyday. I dream about her every week. PLEASE consider keeping your cats indoors only, and even if they are indoor only, always microchip your pets. Those two are my biggest regrets that haunt me when I think of her. The average lifespan of an outdoor cat is 4 years old, and that's how old she was. --------------------------------------------- ***In honor of Foxxy I want to know the names of some amazing animal rescues so I can make a donation in her name. If you know one please comment below and I will choose one next week!**
Inspired by @tal_peleg and of course my cat Foxxy 🐾💕
