Put Your Hand Up to End Violence 🤚 Domestic and Family violence it’s not something that’s easy to talk about. I grew up in a house where I didn’t always feel safe. My Father was a drinker and when he drank you never knew what to expect. Sometimes he was a happy drunk, sometimes maudlin, and other times he was violent. Victoria Against Violence is a 16 day community campaign to call the whole community to action and help prevent family violence and create a safer and more equal Victoria for everyone. It uses orange as a symbol of hope for a future free from violence. The 2017 is “Put Your Hand Up to End Violence 🤚 ” It has one common purpose to end violence against women and children.
Get onboard, share your story and upload your pic using # tags #putyourhandup #goorange #freefromviolence
 @WomenVictoria #ad #speakup #itsnotok #gethelp #reachout

You said you loved me... but you lied... you said you'd protect me... but you lied.. you said you would never hurt me.. but you lied!!! You said you would kill me..you nearly did... This Halloween inspired look was just meant to be a bit of fun..but instead it triggered a lot of memories.. I am a domestic violence survivor, I am a lucky one despite what I went through, other woman aren't so lucky.

P.S I HAVE an amazingly loving husband now that loves and adores me, I am lucky to have him 💖💖💖 Ok back to the light heartered side of things, this was very challenging I threw the wax a few times and chucked a tantrum 🙊🙊 but the end result I am pretty happy! 
