R U D E
.
A while ago @illamasqua blew my mind when they asked me to be part of their #BeyondTheStereotype campaign and then life got in the way and I never managed to create my look. A bit late, but here it is!
I chose their cream blush in the shade Rude because -and I'm sure lots of you ghouls will relate- thanks to my resting bitch face, my makeup, my clothes, my not-always-so-present femininity... People expect me to be rude. As if having certain aesthetics was incompatible with having good manners. Ridiculous, right? It's always a treat to see the faces they make when I approach middle age judgy people at shops and customer services and they go from scared to properly shocked just because I like to use 'sir', 'ma'am' 'please' and 'thank you'. Anyway, I hope that's a way to break that stupid stereotype.
. 
